# What gets committed here is decided by cost to regenerate, not by whether it
# is "generated". We lost the whole phase-4 artifact set once by ignoring all of
# it — the IRs survived in git and were useless without their vocab.
#
# COMMITTED (see the negations below):
#   teacher_data.jsonl  hours of local LLM generation. The expensive one.
#   vocab.json          the student's output labels. The IRs cannot load without it.
#   canonical.json      the dedup map that gives vocab.json its meaning.
#   splits.json         the fingerprinted train/test partition. Reproducibility.
#   student.pt          ~650 KB, same order as the IRs already in git.
#   phase4_results.json the gate results every paper number cites (2026-08-23).
#
# IGNORED: anything rebuildable in seconds from the above.

*.onnx
*.onnx.data
*.log
!phase4_results.json
